X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Billy Crystal: 860
DTSTART:20261020T230000Z
DTEND:20261021T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20261018T074527Z
UID:1009593
DESCRIPTION:<p>In the aftermath of the Palisades fires which took his home
 \, Billy Crystal relives his memories and moments that mattered the most\,
  and how the power of laughter can overcome the most difficult of times. 8
 60 is a hilarious and intimate story about family\, friendship\, love\, lu
 ck\, and loss.<br /><br />Tony&reg\; and Emmy Award&reg\;-winning comedian
 \, actor\, producer\, writer\, and director Billy Crystal is known to audi
 ences around the world as the star of such feature films as <em>When Harry
  Met Sally&hellip\;</em>\, <em>City Slickers</em>\, and <em>Analyze This</
 em>\; as a cast member of NBC&rsquo\;s <em>Saturday Night Live</em>\; and 
 as the acclaimed nine-time host of the Academy Awards&reg\;. He received t
 he Mark Twain Prize for American Humor in 2007\, and in 2023 he was the re
 cipient of a Kennedy Center Honor\, the highest award the United States gi
 ves for the arts. Crystal made his Broadway debut in 2004 with the origina
 l production of his one-man show\, <em>700 Sundays</em>\, for which he won
  a Tony Award.<br /><br />Director Scott Ellis is currently the Interim Ar
 tistic Director of Roundabout Theatre Company. His many Broadway productio
 ns include <em>Fallen Angels</em>\; <em>Art</em>\; <em>Pirates! The Penzan
 ce Musical</em>\; <em>Doubt</em>\; <em>Take Me Out</em> (Tony Award\, Best
  Revival)\; <em>Tootsie</em> (Tony nomination)\; <em>Kiss Me\, Kate</em>\;
  <em>She Loves Me</em> (Tony nomination)\; <em>On the Twentieth Century</e
 m> (Tony nomination)\; <em>Harvey</em>\; <em>Curtains</em> (Tony nominatio
 n)\; <em>The Little Dog Laughed </em>(Drama League Award nomination)\; <em
 >Twelve Angry Men</em> (Tony nomination)\; <em>The Man Who Had All the Luc
 k</em>\; <em>The Rainmaker</em>\; <em>Company</em>\; <em>A Month in the Co
 untry</em>\; and <em>Steel Pier</em> (Tony nomination).</p>
LOCATION:Imperial Theatre\, 249 West 45th Street\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
